{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-29T20:14:54.185Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n**Summary:**\n- `extractCapabilityRules` in `src/harness/types.ts` now accepts an optional `livingSpecsDir`. It drops a delta requirement whose `parseRequirementRules` statement equals the same-titled living requirement's statement. Missing living spec → all rules kept; no directory → unchanged behavior.\n- `resolveCapabilityRules` now resolves the living dir from `projectRoot` + `config.paths.features` (falling back to `openspec/specs`), while an explicit `capabilityRules` (even `[]`) still wins.\n- Added `tests/capability-rules-living.test.ts` covering the scenario through `buildExecutorPrompt`, the no-living-spec case, backward compatibility, and directory resolution.\n\nVerification: task verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/capability-rules-living.test.ts`) passes 8/8; `tests/harness-prompt-injection.test.ts`, function/line budgets, and the full `pnpm verify` (typecheck, build, test suite, biome lint) all pass. Result written to `openspec/changes/116-executor-prompt-fits/.run/results/1.md`."}}
